    "implementedShadowWrite": "AAPL/MSFT/GOOGL/AMZN/NVDA/META/TSLA daily analyst history",
    "behavior": [
      "a pure Java domain policy removes every point for the current UTC date, appends the direct Yahoo consensus point, sorts by date, and retains the latest 365 points",
      "the application use case depends only on current-consensus, legacy-seed, shadow-load, and shadow-save ports",
      "the legacy history is read only when the isolated shadow file is absent; once the shadow exists it is never seeded from legacy again",
      "each ticker is written as the Node-compatible key/updatedAt/value envelope through a same-directory temporary file, file-channel force, and atomic move with a safe fallback",
      "malformed existing shadow data fails closed and per-ticker failures do not stop the remaining batch",
      "striped locks protect concurrent ticker updates and the scheduler overlap guard permits only one batch",
      "the feature is disabled by default and the home shadow compose explicitly enables it with a dedicated named volume",
      "the legacy source-cache bind mount remains read-only and Telegram is never invoked",
      "domain and application contain no Spring, HTTP, Jackson, filesystem, cache-client, controller, or DTO types"
    ],
